[block
  'ORD-0040-order-coherence'
  [ref
    'EMS'
  [/ref]
  [ctx
    'the spec of EMS-002'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/EMS-002.pgml'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'the ratified steps, the measured proposal and the answers of the Regent'
    '.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-ORDER-COHERENCE.md, sections 4, 5, 9, 10 and 11'
  [/ctx]
  [ctx
    'the configuration of a series, which the claim hands the check to'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/ORD-0039'
  [/ctx]
  [tgt
    'step 3 of the trail to the final Explorer, in the Rust only: an Order says where it stands, the Rust reads the claim from its AST, writes it into the manifest as relates, refuses to bundle a claim that does not match, and checks every Order bundled from this one on'
  [/tgt]
  [ins
    'read the claim from the AST, as binds and ref are read: a reference to EMS, to nem, or to an ORD-#### of its own directory, bare or under override, instead-of, deprecated, derive-from or see-also, the relation command naming the kind and its own literals the reason'
  [/ins]
  [ins
    'have the Rust --bundle write relates, one order, kind and reason per claim, and refuse with nothing written when a claim does not match its destination'
  [/ins]
  [ins
    'add glyph --check, which reads every bundle under a folder, holds the Orders bundled from this one on, and answers fix for a mismatch and ask for an Order that makes no claim'
  [/ins]
  [ins
    'run glyph --check over .guidelines/.orders in npm run check'
  [/ins]
  [cnst
    'the trigger is mismatch, not absence: an Order with no claim is asked, never refused'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'the closed Orders are read as emitted, and nothing is asked of them'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'the JS neither extracts relates nor runs the check, and every run of the command line oracle still answers the same bytes in both engines'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'no hash of the snapshot moves; no crate enters'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'npm run check and npm run check:rust green'
  [/cnst]
  [cmp
    'the rules'
    'each mismatch, the absent claim and the cycle of supersession seen refused or asked by a test that failed before the code it holds'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
  [sub
    [eq
      [cmp
        [ctx[/ctx]
      [/cmp]
    [/eq]
  [/sub]
  [elab
    [eq[/eq]
    [sub[/sub]
    [rsn[/rsn]
  [/elab]
  [ref
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/ref]
  [ctx[/ctx]
  [core[/core]
  [core[/core]
  [elab[/elab]
[/block]